    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Terrifying Angels is the seventh studio album by Pure Reason Revolution, a British progressive alternative rock band known for blending lush harmonies, electronic textures, and heavy, dynamic guitar work. Released in 2026 through Inside Out Music with Sony Music involvement, the album continues the band’s post-reunion evolution, pairing expansive songwriting with a more forceful, weighty sound than some of their earlier material.\n\nAcross its seven-track runtime, the record moves between atmospheric introspection and larger, more dramatic passages, with long-form compositions standing alongside shorter, punchier songs. The album also features guest appearances from artists including Mariusz Duda, Paul Mullen, and Kristoffer Gildenlöw, reinforcing its collaborative, progressive spirit. Early reception has highlighted its ambition and intensity, with reviewers noting that it extends the band’s renewed creative momentum rather than revisiting past ideas.",
